# build output
/build/
/build/logs/
obj/

# ★★ GROUND TRUTH IS LOCAL AND NEVER PUSHED (CLAUDE.md §2.2).
# docs/ground-truth/ holds the GIME reference and the AGI Specifications. They are
# third-party documents that live in the working tree and are not ours to redistribute.
# The .gitkeep is tracked (negated below) so the directory exists on a fresh clone and
# a citation like [ref: GIME-RM §10] has a home to point at.
#
# ★ CONSEQUENCE, and it is the reason this is a rule and not a convenience: a citation
# against a file in here is EXECUTOR-VERIFIABLE AND ORCHESTRATOR-UNVERIFIABLE. Absence
# from the public repo is NOT absence from the working tree (CLAUDE.md §2S.2).
docs/ground-truth/*
!docs/ground-truth/.gitkeep

# ★ GAME DATA IS THE USER'S AND IS NEVER COMMITTED (CLAUDE.md §2P).
# games/ holds MANIFESTS ONLY — checksums and version identification. VOL and DIR files
# are copyrighted, are the user's property, and are read-only to this project. A game
# file that reaches the index is a bug, not an oversight.
games/**
!games/manifests/
!games/manifests/.gitkeep
!games/manifests/*.md
!games/manifests/*.json
!games/manifests/*.tsv

# ★ THE ORACLE IS PINNED, NOT VENDORED (CLAUDE.md §2Q.1).
# oracle/ holds oracle/scummvm.pin, patches and dumps. A checked-in ScummVM tree starts
# feeling like source, and per CLAUDE.md §2 there is no source. Never vendor it.
oracle/scummvm/
oracle/src/
oracle/**/*.o
oracle/**/*.so
oracle/**/*.exe

# ★★★ ORACLE DUMPS ARE GAME CONTENT AND WERE NOT IGNORED (found T-P0-028, §2P).
# oracle/dumps/ holds decoded cels, composited frames and 160x168 picture planes -- all of it
# copyrighted and the user's. It was untracked but NOT ignored, which is one `git add -A` away
# from being committed; §2E forbids that command, so the guard held, but a guard that depends on
# never mistyping is not a guard. Same shape as docs/ground-truth/ and games/ above.
# ★ The .gitkeep stays tracked so the directory exists on a fresh clone and oracle_dump.sh has
# somewhere to write.
oracle/dumps/*
!oracle/dumps/.gitkeep

# disk images and build artifacts — reproducible from tools/imgbuild/, never committed
*.dmk
*.dsk
*.jvc
*.vhd
*.bin
!content/*.bin

# python / logs / previews
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
harness/**/previews/
/build/previews/

# MAME writes cfg/ (coco3.cfg, default.cfg) into its CWD, which is the repo root when
# harness/smoke/run_*_test.sh runs. Emulator state, not project state.
/cfg/

# MAME writes snap/ (screenshots) into its CWD, same as cfg/.
/snap/

# MAME rewrites files in -cfg_directory on exit and drops a default.cfg there.
# The authored coco3.cfg templates are tracked; MAME's byproducts are not.
dist/mame-cfg/*/default.cfg

# git checkout-index --temp scratch (used by the .gitattributes CRLF round-trip check)
.merge_file_*


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★ GAME-DATA HARDENING (P0.4) — COMMITTED BEFORE THE CoCo3 CORPUS ARRIVED, DELIBERATELY.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ★★★ THE ORDERING IS THE SAFETY PROPERTY, NOT THE PATTERN LIST.
# Game data pushed to a public repository CANNOT BE DELETED. A later `rm` takes it out of the
# working tree and leaves it in history, and the only real remedy is a history rewrite across
# three synchronised sibling repos (§2M) plus a force-push. So this block landed and was pushed
# BEFORE any archive was dropped into the repo root. Patterns added after the fact protect
# nothing that matters.
#
# This is defence in depth, not the primary control. The primary control is CLAUDE.md §2E's
# explicit-path staging — `git add -A` is forbidden, and this task is the one that earns that
# rule its keep. These patterns catch the case where someone forgets.
#
# ★ NOTE: .gitignore does NOT protect an already-tracked file, and does not stop `git add -f`.
# It stops the accident, not the intent.
#
# --- carrier formats: disk images and archives, AT ANY DEPTH (no leading slash) ------------
*.dsk
*.par
*.zip
*.os9
*.img
*.dmk
*.jvc
*.vhd
*.d77
*.hfe
# not named by the dispatch, added because an archive can arrive in any wrapper:
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.arc
*.lzh
#
# --- AGI resource files by NAME, at any depth ----------------------------------------------
# ★ These have no extension, so an extension rule cannot catch them. They are the actual game
# content: VOL files carry every LOGIC, PICTURE, VIEW and SOUND resource; the DIR files index
# them; words.tok is the parser vocabulary; object is the inventory table.
vol.*
*vol.[0-9]
*VOL.[0-9]
logdir
picdir
viewdir
snddir
words.tok
object
# OS-9 table-of-contents shipped on the Sierra disks (spelled tOC / tOC.txt / toc / toc.txt)
[Tt][Oo][Cc]
[Tt][Oo][Cc].txt
LOGDIR
PICDIR
VIEWDIR
SNDDIR
WORDS.TOK
OBJECT
# v3 combined-directory shapes (<prefix>dir, e.g. dmdir / vdir — P0.3 §4.2).
# ★ Deliberately broad: a v3 title names its directory file after its own prefix, so the set of
# possible names is open-ended and cannot be enumerated. The cost is that a future directory
# whose name ends in "dir" would also be ignored; the benefit is that no v3 title can slip
# through on a prefix nobody predicted. Safety wins here — and an intended file can always be
# added with `git add -f`, which is a visible act.
*dir
*Dir
*DIR
# ★★ THE MIXED CASE IS NOT DEFENSIVENESS, IT IS THE MEASURED FILENAME. The CoCo3 corpus names
# these files `logDir`, `picDir`, `viewDir`, `sndDir` -- capital D, lower-case rest -- and
# `*dir` would NOT match that on a case-sensitive filesystem. It matched here only because this
# Windows host compares case-insensitively, which is a property of the host and not of the rule.
# Found by reading the actual OS-9 directory entries at P0.4, not by guessing.
#
# --- Sierra's CoCo3 interpreter and OS-9 modules -------------------------------------------
# ★ Sierra's shipped interpreter is COPYRIGHTED CODE, not game data, and is likewise never
# committed. It is a comparison target only (dispatch §7 / backlog D-14).
CMDS/
MODULES/
OS9Boot
os9boot
#
# --- DOS/PC releases (P1.1) -----------------------------------------------------------------
# ★ The AGI resource names above already cover the DOS forms — LOGDIR/VOL.0/WORDS.TOK/OBJECT
# are matched by the uppercase and vol.* rules, verified by check-ignore before the drop. What
# they do NOT cover is everything else a DOS release ships, all of it equally copyrighted:
#
#   Sierra's interpreter and its drivers — .EXE/.COM/.OVL/.DRV/.SYS
*.exe
*.EXE
*.com
*.COM
*.ovl
*.OVL
*.drv
*.DRV
*.sys
*.SYS
#   Game text, help, screens and art shipped beside the resources
*.qa
*.QA
*.msg
*.MSG
*.scr
*.SCR
*.hlp
*.HLP
*.gif
*.GIF
#
# ★★ SCI GAME DATA. Some "King's Quest" directories are SCI, not AGI (design §1.1 puts SCI out
# of scope entirely). Out of scope does NOT mean safe to commit — it is still the user's game.
# Named exactly rather than as *.map, because a linker map is legitimate build output and a
# blanket rule would quietly swallow one.
RESOURCE.MAP
RESOURCE.map
resource.map
RESOURCE.[0-9][0-9][0-9]
resource.[0-9][0-9][0-9]
RESOURCE.AGI
RESOURCE.SFX
#
# ★ NOT IGNORED, DELIBERATELY: *.bat. A DOS release ships one, but `build.bat` is this
# project's build contract (CLAUDE.md §1) and .gitattributes pins it to CRLF because cmd.exe
# cannot parse an LF-only batch. A blanket *.bat rule would make the eventual build.bat
# un-addable without `git add -f`. §2E's explicit-path staging is the control here, as it is
# everywhere else — this block is defence in depth, not the primary guard.

# ★★ WHAT IS STILL ALLOWED THROUGH, and must stay allowed:
#   games/manifests/*.tsv  — checksums, sizes and version identification. NEVER content.
# That negation lives in the games/** block above and is not overridden here: no pattern in
# this section matches a .tsv, a .md or a .json.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ORACLE RUNTIME DROPPINGS (P4.2)
#
# ★ ScummVM writes its configuration file into the PROCESS WORKING DIRECTORY. Since P4.2 the
# oracle is a native Windows binary that gets invoked from wherever the shell happens to be,
# so running it with the repo as CWD drops a scummvm.ini here. Observed exactly that way.
#
# It arrived empty, but a populated one records GAME PATHS pointing into the user's corpus.
# That is not game data (§2P) and is not dangerous, but it is machine-local state that has no
# business being tracked, and the file reappears every time the oracle is run from the repo.
# Ignored rather than deleted-and-forgotten, because deleting it does not stop it coming back.
#
# ★ oracle_dump.sh is NOT the source of these: it cd's to the output directory first, which is
# precisely why it does that. Ad-hoc invocations are the source.
scummvm.ini
scummvm.log

# MAME save states: machine snapshots, never tracked (CLAUDE.md 2P)
sta/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★ DOS-RELEASE HARDENING (P1.4) — COMMITTED AND PUSHED BEFORE THE ARCHIVES ARRIVE.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ★★★ THE ORDERING IS THE SAFETY PROPERTY, exactly as the P0.4 block above says. Six archives
# with nine AGI v2 titles are about to be dropped in the repo root. Everything below landed and
# was PUSHED first, and `harness/tools/ignore_probe.py` proves each case with
# `git check-ignore -v` rather than by reading the patterns and believing them (L-28).
#
# ★ The P0.4 block already covers the AGI resource names, the archive formats in circulation
# then, the DOS interpreter/driver/text extensions and the SCI resource files. What follows is
# only what the probe found MISSING for a DOS drop.
#
# --- archive wrappers P0.4 did not anticipate ----------------------------------------------
# ★ An Internet Archive upload arrives in whatever the uploader used. .cab and .iso are both
# common for DOS-era bundles and neither was covered.
*.cab
*.CAB
*.iso
*.ISO
*.ace
*.ACE
*.zoo
*.ZOO
*.dms
*.adf
#
# --- ★★★ BATCH FILES: THE ONE THE P0.4 BLOCK DELIBERATELY LEFT OUT -------------------------
# ★★ P0.4 declined a blanket *.bat and SAID WHY: `build.bat` is CLAUDE.md §1's build contract,
# .gitattributes pins it to CRLF because cmd.exe cannot parse an LF-only batch, and a blanket
# rule would make it un-addable without `git add -f`. That reasoning was right and is preserved
# — the rule below is not a reversal, it is the same rule with the exception made explicit.
#
# ★★★ Every DOS AGI release ships one (SIERRA.BAT, INSTALL.BAT), so the gap is real now in a way
# it was not when the CoCo3 corpus was the only thing arriving. The negation is anchored to the
# REPOSITORY ROOT (`/build.bat`), so this project's build contract stays addable and a batch file
# anywhere else — which is where a dropped release would put one — is caught.
*.bat
*.BAT
!/build.bat
#
# ★ Sibling repos keep their own build.bat at their own root; this file is not shared (§2M lists
# the ten shared HAL files and .gitignore is not among them), so the anchoring is local.
